From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] configs: orangepi_zero2: talk to the AXP305 over RSB

The Zero2 device tree puts the AXP305 on r_rsb (pmic@745); TF-A and
Linux use RSB and the PMIC stays in RSB mode across warm reboots, so the
SPL's R_I2C access fails on every reboot ("Failed to set core voltage!
Can't set CPU frequency", CPU left at 408 MHz until Linux cpufreq).
Use the RSB controller in the SPL instead; drop the now unused legacy
mvtwsi R_I2C setup. CONFIG_SPL_I2C stays, it pulls drivers/i2c (the RSB
driver) into the SPL build.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
--- a/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
+++ b/configs/orangepi_zero2_defconfig
@@ -9,16 +9,12 @@ CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR6=0x33808080
 CONFIG_DRAM_SUNXI_TPR10=0xf83438
 CONFIG_MACH_SUN50I_H616=y
 CONFIG_SUNXI_DRAM_H616_DDR3_1333=y
-CONFIG_R_I2C_ENABLE=y
 CONFIG_SPL_SPI_SUNXI=y
 CONFIG_SPL_SUNXI_LED_STATUS=y
 CONFIG_SPL_SUNXI_LED_STATUS_GPIO=76
 # CONFIG_SYS_MALLOC_CLEAR_ON_INIT is not set
 CONFIG_SPL_I2C=y
-CONFIG_SPL_SYS_I2C_LEGACY=y
-CONFIG_SYS_I2C_MVTWSI=y
-CONFIG_SYS_I2C_SLAVE=0x7f
-CONFIG_SYS_I2C_SPEED=400000
+CONFIG_SYS_I2C_SUN8I_RSB=y
 CONFIG_MTD=y
 CONFIG_SPI_FLASH_MACRONIX=y
 CONFIG_SUN8I_EMAC=y
